      "license": "CC BY-SA 2.0",
      "licenseUrl": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/2.0",
      "artist": "Trish Steel",
      "description": "High Street, Tuam/Tuaim Despite its 19th century air, the large market town of Tuam (pronounced 'choom') has a long history.  A monastery was founded here in the early 6th century, and in the 11th century the O'Conor kings of Connaught made it their base.  Two of them, Turlough and Ruari, became High Kings and in their times Tuam was effectively Ireland's capital.",
